**Proposer:** Ganesha
**Date:** 2026-03-12
**Type:** Bug Fix
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)
**ID:** IMVAO

## Summary

Willow and all non-shiva/kart agents hallucinate on factual questions because
(a) context injection is gated to only 3 agents, and (b) RAG only fires on
keyword-matched "retrieval queries." Most questions get zero knowledge base
grounding. Fix: extend context injection to all agents, make RAG default-on
with casual as the only exclusion.

## Root Cause

Two independent gates both prevent RAG from firing:

**Gate 1 — agent_engine.py line 183:**
```python
if self.agent_name in ("shiva", "kart", "sean"):
    memory_header = context_injector.build_context_header(...)
```
Willow, Ada, Gerald, Riggs, Steve get no memory injection.

**Gate 2 — local_api.py line 1128:**
```python
retrieval_signals = ["history", "remember", "discussed", "said", "mentioned",
                     "last time", "previous", "earlier"]
is_retrieval_query = any(kw in retrieval_signals for kw in keywords)
if not is_casual and is_retrieval_query:
    retrieved = search_knowledge(prompt)
```
RAG only fires if the prompt contains those exact keywords. "What's the status
of the installer?" gets no RAG. "What did we decide about Tauri?" gets RAG.
The distinction is arbitrary and causes consistent hallucination on factual
questions that don't use retrieval phrasing.

## Proposed Changes

### File 1: core/agent_engine.py
**Location:** lines 183-187 (inside `chat()`, context injection block)

**Before:**
```python
if self.agent_name in ("shiva", "kart", "sean"):
    memory_header = context_injector.build_context_header(
        self.username, self.agent_name, user_message=user_message
    )
    system_content = memory_header + "\n\n" + system_content
```

**After:**
```python
memory_header = context_injector.build_context_header(
    self.username, self.agent_name, user_message=user_message
)
if memory_header:
    system_content = memory_header + "\n\n" + system_content
```

**Rationale:** `build_context_header` already accepts any agent_name. The
agent-name gate was never justified — it was a conservative default that became
the permanent behavior. All agents should have access to memory.

---

### File 2: local_api.py
**Location:** lines 1119-1135 (inside `process_smart_stream()`, RAG block)

**Before:**
```python
retrieved = ""
if force_tier is None:
    keywords = extract_keywords(prompt)
    retrieval_signals = ["history", "remember", "discussed", "said", "mentioned",
                         "last time", "previous", "earlier"]
    is_retrieval_query = any(kw in retrieval_signals for kw in keywords)

    if not is_casual and is_retrieval_query:
        retrieved = search_knowledge(prompt)
        if retrieved and len(retrieved) > 300:
            _log(f"RAG_INJECT | retrieval query, adding context to tier {tier}")
    elif is_casual:
        _log(f"TIER_CASUAL | casual question at Tier {tier}, skipping RAG")
    else:
        _log(f"TIER_NORMAL | message at Tier {tier}")
```

**After:**
```python
retrieved = ""
if force_tier is None:
    if is_casual:
        _log(f"TIER_CASUAL | casual question at Tier {tier}, skipping RAG")
    else:
        retrieved = search_knowledge(prompt)
        if retrieved and len(retrieved) > 300:
            _log(f"RAG_INJECT | grounding context added for tier {tier}")
        else:
            _log(f"TIER_NORMAL | no matching context found, tier {tier}")
```

**Rationale:** Invert the logic. RAG is now default-on for all non-casual
prompts. The keyword-based `is_retrieval_query` check was the hallucination
source — it excluded most factual questions. Casual exclusion (greetings,
preferences, roleplay) is still respected.

Also: extract_and_store gating in line 245 is left as-is (shiva/kart/sean only)
since that writes to memory, not reads from it — a separate decision.

## Rationale

Agents answering from model weights alone about Willow-specific state (tasks,
decisions, open work, session history) will always hallucinate. The knowledge
base exists precisely to ground these answers. Both gates preventing that
grounding are bugs, not features.

## Risk Assessment
Risk Level: LOW
Reversible: YES
Dependencies: context_injector.build_context_header() handles unknown agent
names gracefully (confirmed: accepts any string, returns "" if no context found).
search_knowledge() is already in production use on retrieval queries — no new
code path, just broader invocation.

Potential side effect: slightly higher latency on non-casual prompts due to
knowledge search on every call. Acceptable given hallucination is the current
alternative.
